An item can normally have one influence type at a time and newly dropped influenced items will always have at least one influenced affix when acquired. Modifying the item will not guarantee an influence modifier.

It is possible to create items with ''two'' influences by using {{il|Awakener's Orb}}: the orb will destroy an item and transfer its influence type to a different item. This last item will have two different influence types as a result. Currently there are 15 combinations (6 combinations of 2). The order of the donor item does not affect the order of the influence icon on the final item, for example using an Elder item as a donor and a Shaper item as receiver of the mods yields the same influence set as using a Shaper item as donor and an Elder item as receiver. The item has a fixed order of influence icons. Additionally, some unique items will naturally drop with both Shaper and Elder influences, like {{il|Voidfletcher}}.

{{il|Astrolabe Amulet|Astrolabe Amulets}} count as having all six influences.

There are [[List of influence adding items|currency items]] that add a modifier from their influence mod pool to the item. This cannot be done if the item already has an influence different than the orb being applied.

Items retain their influences when modified, even if an {{il|Orb of Scouring}} is used. It is possible to create certain [[unique item]]s on an already influenced item using {{il|Orb of Chance|Orbs of Chance}} or {{il|Tainted Mythic Orb|Tainted Mythic Orbs}}. [[Vendor recipe]]s that create unique items will create an influenced item if the equipment used for the recipe have the same influence. These influenced unique items can be used to satisfy the condition of unique items with effects that require other influenced items equipped to activate, such as {{il|The Eternity Shroud}}, {{il|Bound by Destiny}}, and {{il|Venarius' Astrolabe}}.

[[Fractured item]]s, [[synthesised item]]s and items with [[eldritch implicit modifier]]s are not considered influenced and cannot be given influences under any circumstances. Conversely, influenced items cannot be fractured or synthesised, or have [[eldritch currency]] applied to them (though it was possible to create a fractured influenced item in [[Necropolis league]] via [[The Necropolis|Necropolis]] crafting). They also cannot be [[Split (item modifier)|split]].

By using a [[Horticrafting Station]] [[Harvest crafting|Harvest craft]] for 1000 {{il|Primal Crystallised Lifeforce}}, it is possible to randomise the influence types on an influenced non-unique item, while reforging the item with new random modifiers.

A full set of gear with the same influence can be sold to a [[vendor]] for one {{il|Exalted Orb}}, two if all the gear is unidentified.

==Crusader item==
{{see also|List of crusader modifiers}}
'''Crusader items''' are dropped by [[Baran, the Crusader]] or rarely from monsters and chests of map under his influence. They can also drop while under the effects of a [[Shrine#Apparition|Crusader's Shrine]]. It can be crafted by using a {{il|Crusader's Exalted Orb}}. They can be recognized by their electric outline and [[File:Crusader-item-symbol.png]] symbols next to the item's name.

*Prefix: {{c|mod|Crusader's}}
*Suffix: {{c|mod|of the Crusade}}

==Hunter item==
{{see also|List of hunter modifiers}}
'''Hunter items''' are dropped by [[Al-Hezmin, the Hunter]] or rarely from monsters and chests of map under his influence. They can also drop while under the effects of a [[Shrine#Apparition|Hunter's Shrine]]. It can be crafted by using a {{il|Hunter's Exalted Orb}}. They can be recognized by their poisonous outline and [[File:Hunter-item-symbol.png]] symbols next to the item's name.

*Prefix: {{c|mod|Hunter's}}
*Suffix: {{c|mod|of the Hunt}}

==Redeemer item==
{{see also|List of redeemer modifiers}}
'''Redeemer items''' are dropped by [[Veritania, the Redeemer]] or rarely from monsters and chests of map under her influence. They can also drop while under the effects of a [[Shrine#Apparition|Redeemer's Shrine]]. It can be crafted by using a {{il|Redeemer's Exalted Orb}}. They can be recognized by their sparkly outline and [[File:Redeemer-item-symbol.png]] symbols next to the item's name.

*Prefix: {{c|mod|Redeemer's}}
*Suffix: {{c|mod|of Redemption}}

==Warlord item==
{{see also|List of warlord modifiers}}
'''Warlord items''' are dropped by [[Drox, the Warlord]], or rarely from monsters and chests of map under his influence. They can also drop while under the effects of a [[Shrine#Apparition|Warlord's Shrine]]. It can be crafted by using a {{il|Warlord's Exalted Orb}}. They can be recognized by their blazing outline and [[File:Warlord-item-symbol.png]] symbols next to the item's name.

*Prefix: {{c|mod|Warlord's}}
*Suffix: {{c|mod|of the Conquest}}

==Shaper item==
[[File:Shaped item example.png|thumb|400px|An example of a rare Shaper item]]
{{see also|List of shaper modifiers}}
'''Shaper items''' are found in Shaper-influenced maps or dropped by [[the Shaper]] and [[Uber Shaper]] (and including [[Uber Elder]] fight, which most drops from that fight is dual Shaper-Elder influenced), with the exception of {{il|Replica Voidwalker}}. It can be crafted by using a {{il|Shaper's Exalted Orb}}. They can be recognized by their cosmic background and [[File:Shaper-item-symbol.png]] symbols next to the item's name. Other methods of acquiring Shaper items include Shaper [[Scarab]]s, [[Delve]] rewards and [[Incubator]]s.

*Prefix: {{c|mod|The Shaper's}}
*Suffix: {{c|mod|of Shaping}}

Shaper-influenced maps can be sold or offered as a mission by [[Commander Kirac|Kirac]]. The map item would have an implicit {{c|mod|Area is influenced by The Shaper}}.

